  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Natural talent for opening and filling an aperture is graded on a four-step scale from A down to D. B grade sits just below A grade on that scale. Clan talk already treats a B grade result as worth heavy care: the youth is often raised toward a future clan elder seat.",
      "chapters": [
        4
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "On Qing Mao Mountain, the Awakening Ceremony measures talent by how far a fifteen-year-old walks into the moon orchid flower sea while Hope Gu enter the body. Fang Yuan states the bands used there: below ten steps means no cultivation talent, ten to twenty is D grade, twenty to thirty C grade, thirty to forty B grade, and forty to fifty A grade.",
      "chapters": [
        5
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "how-the-grade-is-measured",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_qing_mao_mountain",
        "gu_hope_gu",
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Gu Yue Mo Bei walks thirty-six steps and is named a B grade talent on the spot. The academy elder checks his aperture and records a primeval sea measuring six by six, fit for vigorous training. Fake results can also wear the B grade label: Gu Yue Chi Chen later walks the same thirty-six steps in public while, in Fang Yuan’s memory, his true grade is only C grade under his grandfather’s help.",
      "chapters": [
        4
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "how-the-grade-is-measured",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_gu_yue_mo_bei",
        "char_gu_yue_chi_cheng"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The grade governs how much of the aperture the primeval sea fills, and therefore how much essence the Gu Master holds and how fast that essence recovers.",
      "chapters": [
        7
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "what-b-grade-governs",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_master"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The academy elder states that a B grade talent’s primeval sea takes up six to seven layers of the aperture, and that this talent can cultivate to rank three, even as far as rank four.",
      "chapters": [
        7
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "what-b-grade-governs",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Clan expectation talk earlier says a B grade youth must be cared for, often becoming a future clan elder, and with six to seven years of training will become a rank three Gu Master.",
      "chapters": [
        4
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "what-b-grade-governs",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Branch elders treat that height as decisive in academy rivalry. Gu Yue Mo Chen’s side argues that Mo Bei’s B grade, with family support, should eventually step over a C grade peer such as Fang Yuan.",
      "chapters": [
        31
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "what-b-grade-governs",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_gu_yue_mo_chen"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Advancement-pace talk later places a C grade youth at about twice a B grade, and four times an A grade, when rising to middle stage on talent alone.",
      "chapters": [
        50
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "what-b-grade-governs",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Primeval stones can still close part of the gap: with enough stones, a B grade can outpace an A grade in a vital Gu refinement contest.",
      "chapters": [
        8
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "what-b-grade-governs",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_vital_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Talent grades sit beside the aperture mechanics on aperture and primeval essence. The ceremony that produces the grade is on Awakening Ceremony. The full ladder is on Aptitude.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "what-b-grade-governs",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_aptitude",
        "sys_aperture_and_primeval_essence",
        "sys_awakening_ceremony"
      ]
    }
  ],
